From 341cb53afc07f0a1ca78cdcc9267421ea89239ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 01:52:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: widen the download-key ADC window for 12-bit
 SARADCs

rockchip_dnl_key_pressed() treats the SARADC channel-1 sample as a key
press only when the raw value is within 0..30. That window was sized for
the 10-bit SARADCs on older SoCs; RK3576 binds the 12-bit rk3588_saradc
data, so the same grounded-key voltage lands about four times higher in
raw counts. On this hardware a pressed recovery/jack button reads raw ~41
(about 18 mV) -- just outside the 0..30 window -- so the key is sampled
correctly yet reported as unpressed, and the BootROM-download path never
fires. Widen KEY_DOWN_MAX_VAL to 100 (about 44 mV against the 1.8 V
reference): far below the ~4087 idle level, comfortably capturing the
press. Pairs with matching the SARADC by driver, which makes the device
findable in the first place.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
index be131b80..2600fd20 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/boot_mode.c
@@ -35,7 +35,7 @@ void set_back_to_bootrom_dnl_flag(void)
  * some special boards.
  */
 #define KEY_DOWN_MIN_VAL	0
-#define KEY_DOWN_MAX_VAL	30
+#define KEY_DOWN_MAX_VAL	100
 
 __weak int rockchip_dnl_key_pressed(void)
 {
-- 
2.43.0

